{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/28052-mummy-xp-system-and-consistency-with-the-gmc-update","id":28052,"title":"Mummy XP system and consistency with the GMC update","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-11T09:32:58-08:00","id":28052,"title":"Mummy XP system and consistency with the GMC update","content":"Has someone released an FAQ on how the GMC update impacts XP costs of things like Affinities for Mummy? Also how does the across the board XP cost reduction from GMC impact the extra XP that Mummy characters start with?<br /> <br /> Thanks, any insights you all provide will be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:56:04-08:00","id":28063,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, the general guidelines I recall were that 1 experience in the Chronicle system \u2248 5 XP in the old Storytelling System, with scaling dot costs based approximately on the cost of a three-dot purchase in the old system, and a general bias towards making supernatural powers a little more affordable.<br /> <br /> Taking that into mind, and cracking open my corebook, I'd venture something like...<br /> <br /> Start with 10 Merit dots instead of 7.<br /> Start with 5 free experiences.<br /> 1 experience for a dot of a defining pillar<br /> 2 experiences for a dot of another pillar<br /> 3 experiences for a favored or fated affinity<br /> 4 experiences for an unfavored affinity<br /> 3 experiences for an utterance<br /> 3 experiences or 1 sebayt experience for a dot of Memory<br /> 1 experience to recover a lost dot of Willpower<br /> When you would normally award sebayt XP, instead award one sebayt beat. Convert 10 sebayt beats into 1 sebayt experience, which can be spent to improve Memory.<br /> <br /> Good luck improvising freestyle Virtue and Vice effects for the powers that cite the original seven Virtues and seven Vices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:01:23-08:00","id":28286,"title":"","content":"The previous forum had <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default8122.html?g=posts&amp;t=73406\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a> (link leads to the archive), which lists a number of hacks to convert Mummy to the GMC rules.<br /> <br /> Remember that those rules were still under discussion when the old forum dissapeared, so use common sensen when applying them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T11:11:31-08:00","id":41208,"title":"","content":"Thanks for these tips. They have been very helpful. I'm sharing some GMC update house rules below in case anyone finds them helpful.<br /> <br /> Updating Memory, Virtue, &amp; Vice to better align with GMC's Integrity and B&amp;S's Humanity<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><i>Remembrance</i></b> replaces <b><i>Virtue</i></b>. This is a defining characteristic from the Mummy\u2019s past self. Regain 1 Willpower by pursuing knowledge that would shed light on who she was during the time of ancient Irem. Regain all Willpower once per story by taking a great risk to regain some token of her past.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Authority</i></b> replaces <b><i>Vice</i></b>. This is a defining characteristic of the Mummy as an agent of the Judges of Duat. Regains 1 Willpower by acting in accord to her Judge\u2019s archetype. Regain all Willpower once per story by taking actions to further her Judge\u2019s agenda that put her at very great risk.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Memory</i></b>: The morality stat in Mummy, begins at 3. Sins are replaced by <b><i>Breaking Points</i></b>. Mummies are penalized for having low <i>Memory</i> scores and rewarded for having high scores.<ul><li><b>Enlightened (Memory 9-10): </b>Gains the Eidetic Memory and Unseen Sense (Judges of Duat) Merits. These merits are lost should the Mummy\u2019s <i>Memory</i> dip below 9.</li> <li><b>Clear-headed (Memory 7-8): </b>(as Memory 8 in the M:tC rulebook).</li> <li><b>Inattentive (Memory 5-6): </b>Rolls to interact with humans are at -1. Meditation rolls are reduced by -1 when outside of Tomb.</li> <li><b>Oblivious (Memory 4): </b>Rolls to interact with humans are at -1 and rolls to interact with technology (through certain Mental skills) are at -1. Meditation rolls are reduced by -2 when outside of Tomb.</li> <li><b>Confused (Memory 3): </b>Rolls to interact with humans are at -2 and rolls to interact with technology (through certain Mental skills) are at -1. Meditation rolls are reduced by -3 when outside of Tomb.</li> <li><b>Amnesic (Memory 2): </b>Rolls to interact with humans are at -3 and rolls to interact with technology (through certain Mental skills) are at -2. Meditation rolls are at reduced by -5 when outside of Tomb.</li> <li><b>Senescent (Memory 1): </b>Rolls to interact with humans are at -5 and rolls to interact with technology (through certain Mental skills) are at -3. Meditation rolls are reduced to a luck die when outside of Tomb.</li> <li><b>Akhu (Memory 0): </b>(as in the M:tC rulebook)</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tweaks for Sybaris<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Sybaris Effects:</b><ul><li><b>Terror Sybaris </b>(as in M:tC, resisted by Composure + Resolve roll)<ul><li><b>Dramatic Failure </b>\u2013 Mortal gains the Frightened Condition</li> <li><b>Failure \u2013 </b>Mortal gains the Spooked Condition</li> <li><b>Success \u2013 </b>Mortal gains the Shaken Condition</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Unease Sybaris </b>(as in M:tC; degree equal to Memory - Sekhem)<ul><li><b>-8 or less </b>\u2013 Mortal gains the Enervated Condition</li> <li><b>-7 to -5 </b>\u2013 Mortal gains the Soulless Condition</li> <li><b>-4 to -3 </b>\u2013 Mortal gains the Obsession Condition</li> <li><b>-2 to -1 \u2013 </b>Mortal gains the Delusional Condition</li> <li><b>0 </b>\u2013 Mortal gains the Spooked Condition</li> <li><b>+1 </b>\u2013 Mortal gains the Shaken Condition</li> <li><b>+2 or more </b>\u2013 Mortal is immune to the effects of Unease Sybaris</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Experiences<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Experience Costs:</b><ul><li>Attributes: 3 / dot</li> <li>Merits: 1 / dot</li> <li>Skills: 2 / dot</li> <li>Skill Specialties: 1 each</li> <li>Defining Pillar: 1 / dot</li> <li>Other Pillars: 2 / dot</li> <li>Favored or Fated Affinities: 4 each</li> <li>Other Affinities: 5 each</li> <li>Utterances: 5 each</li> <li>Memory: 3 / dot</li> <li>Willpower: 1 / dot</li> </ul><b>Bonus Experiences:</b><ul><li><b>Starting Character </b>\u2013 5 experience points</li> <li><b>Around the Block \u2013 </b>10 experience points</li> <li><b>Rising Star </b>\u2013 15 experience points</li> <li><b>Acclimated Arisen </b>\u2013 20 experience points</li> <li><b>Descent Veteran \u2013 </b>30 experience points</li> <li><b>Mover and Shaker \u2013 </b>40 experience points</li> <li><b>Urban Legend</b> \u2013 55 experience points</li> <li><b>Legendary Immortal \u2013 </b>105 experience points</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sekhem uses, changed time scale for Descent rolls forced due to time active.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><i>Sekhem:</i></b><ul><li><b>Attribute/Skill/Power Maximum</b> (as in rulebook)</li> <li><b>Descent Rolls </b>(pool as in rulebook but rolling conditions as follows)<ul><li><b>Time: </b><ul><li>Sekhem 10 \u2013 roll after 7 days (failure adds 3 days)</li> <li>Sekhem 9 \u2013 roll after 7 days (failure adds 3 days)</li> <li>Sekhem 8 \u2013 roll after 7 days (failure adds 3 days)</li> <li>Sekhem 7 \u2013 roll after 7 weeks (failure adds 3 weeks)</li> <li>Sekhem 6 \u2013 roll after 7 weeks (failure adds 3 weeks)</li> <li>Sekhem 5 \u2013 roll after 7 weeks (failure adds 3 weeks)</li> <li>Sekhem 4 \u2013 roll after 7 months (failure adds 3 months)</li> <li>Sekhem 3 \u2013 roll after 7 months (failure adds 3 months)</li> <li>Sekhem 2 \u2013 roll after 7 months (failure adds 3 months)</li> <li>Sekhem 1 \u2013 roll after 7 years (failure adds 3 years)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Sins against Duat: </b>(as in M:tC rulebook, p. 155)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Effortless Power</b> (as in M:tC rulebook)</li> <li><b>Lifesense</b>: Can detect Sekhem (as per <i>kepher</i> in the M:tC rulebook)</li> <li><b>Possession Immunity</b> (as in M:tC rulebook; works against the Strix too)</li> <li><b>Repairing the Sahu:</b> Can sacrifice one dot of <i>Sekhem</i> per turn to repair one level of aggravated damage.</li> <li><b>Unclean Remains </b>(as in rulebook)</li> <li><b>Undeath </b>(as in rulebook)</li> <li><b>Using Third Tier <i>Utterances </i></b>(see Utterances below)</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Affinity Changes<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Affinities</b><ul><li>Replace any <i>Willpower </i>expenditures with the <i>Pillar</i> of the appropriate type for <i>Pillar Affinities</i>, use the character\u2019s <i>Defining Pillar</i> for expenditures on <i>Guild Affinities</i>.</li> <li>Ignore any mechanics linked to <i>Virtues</i> or <i>Vices</i> except as noted below.</li> <li><b><i>Affinities </i></b>(Note that many <i>Affinities</i> operate well without any changes (except for substituting <i>Pillars </i>for <i>Willpower</i>). <i>Affinities</i> listed below required major revisions due to use of derangements or <i>Vice/Virtue</i> mechanics.)<ul><li><b>Ancient Horror Unveiling: </b>Target is affected by the Spooked Condition. If the target\u2019s resistance roll is a dramatic failure he is affected by the Frightened Condition instead.</li> <li><b>Fearsome Soul:</b> Replace <i>Vice</i> with <i>Authority</i> and <i>Virtue</i> with <i>Remembrance</i>.</li> <li><b>Nihilist Awakening:</b> Target is affected by the Broken Condition. If the target\u2019s resistance roll is a dramatic failure he is affected by the Fugue Condition instead.</li> <li><b>Paragon Shames the Weak:</b> Targets are affected by the Humbled Condition.</li> <li><b>Radiant Lifeforce:</b> May suffer 1 point of Aggravated damage to remove the Broken, Enervated, Fugue, Madness, Obsession, or Soulless Condition from herself. She gains the Lethargic Condition.</li> <li><b>Rouse the Khaibit: </b>Replace <i>Vice</i> with <i>Authority</i> and <i>Virtue</i> with <i>Remembrance</i>.</li> <li><b>Soul Infusion:</b> Use of this <i>Affinity</i> to drain <i>Willpower</i> causes the target to gain the Soulless Condition. If the target is already affected by the Soulless Condition then they gain the Enervated Condition instead. This <i>Affinity</i> cannot be used on targets suffering from the Enervated Condition.</li> <li><b>Voice of Conscience:</b> Target is affected by the Inspired Condition.</li> <li><b>Voice of Temptation:</b> Target is affected by the Leveraged Condition.</li> <li><b>Wisdom from Ruin: </b>Ignore the first ability of this <i>Affinity </i>altogether.</li> <li><b>Words Summoned Forth:</b> Target is affected by the Obsession Condition. If the target\u2019s resistance roll is a dramatic failure, he is affected by the Delusional Condition instead.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Utterance Changes<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Utterances</b><ul><li><b>First Tier: </b>Costs 1 <i>Pillar </i>of any type.</li> <li><b>Second Tier:</b> Costs as First Tier +1 <i>Pillar</i> of any type listed in the Utterance\u2019s description.</li> <li><b>Third Tier:</b> Costs as Second Tier + 1 additional <i>Pillar </i>of another type listed must be spent, 1 <i>Willpower</i> must be spent, or 1 <i>Sekhem</i> must be sacrificed. (See notes below.)</li> <li>Ignore any mechanics linked to <i>Virtues</i> or <i>Vices </i>except as noted below.</li> <li><b><i>Utterances:</i></b><ul><li><b>Ancestry of Forgotten Stars: </b>Tier 3 costs each Hierophant the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Awaken the Dead:</b> Tier 3 costs additional sacrificed <i>Sekhem</i> (1 dot = Memory + Sekhem hours duration, 2 dots = Memory + Sekhem days duration, 3 dots = Memory + Sekhem weeks duration, 4 dots = Memory + Sekhem months duration, 5 dots = Memory + Sekhem years duration)</li> <li><b>Blessed is the God-King: </b>Tier 1 causes the Arisen to be affected by the Steadfast Condition. Tier 2 causes the target to be affected by the Inspired Condition. Tier 3 cost is the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Bound as Fingers in a Fist:</b> Tier 3 cost is 1 additional <i>Pillar (Ka</i>,<i> Ren, </i>or<i> Ba)</i>. Ignore all mentions of changing victim\u2019s <i>Virtues</i> and <i>Vices</i>.</li> <li><b>Cthonic Dominion:</b> Tier 3 cost is an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Command the Beasts: </b>Tier 3 cost is an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Discipline the Obstinate: </b>Tier 3 cost is the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Doom Affliction: </b>Tier 3 cost is 1 additional <i>Pillar (Ab</i>,<i> Ka,</i> or<i> Ba)</i>.</li> <li><b>Dreams of Dead Gods: </b>Tier 1 causes the victims to be affected by the Confused or Distracted Condition. Tier 2 causes the target to be affected by either the Shaken or the Swooning Condition. Tier 3 cost is an additional 1 <i>Willpower </i>and causes the target to be affected by the Soulless, Charmed, or Tasked Condition.</li> <li><b>Dust Beneath Feet:</b> Tier 3 cost is the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Gift of the Golden Ankh:</b> Tier 3 cost is an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Harvest the Divine Flesh: </b>Tier 1 causes the target to be affected by the Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, or Leg Wrack Tilts. Tier 3 cost is the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Inscription of Flesh:</b> Tier 2 first effect is changed so that it can be used to cause or cure a Disease in the target. Targets affected by a Disease suffer the effects of the \u201cGrave\u201d Sick Tilt. Tier 3 first effect is changed so that it can be used to kill ordinary mortals instantly. Mages, Hunters, Sin-Eaters, mortals with Supernatural Merits, and mortals under the effects of supernatural Conditions are immune. Damage inflicted to Prometheans by the second Tier 3 effect is Lethal rather than Aggravated. The fourth Tier 3 effect can be used to add or remove the Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, Insensate, or Leg Wrack Tilts to the target. Tier 3 cost is an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Jar of Clay: </b>No changes from M:tC\u2019s GotD.</li> <li><b>Jar of Teeth: </b>Tier 3 cost is the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Kiss of Apep:</b> Tier 3 costs 1 additional <i>Pillar (Ren</i>,<i> Ka, </i>or<i> Sheut)</i>.</li> <li><b>Mastery of Heka\u2019s Bounty: </b>Tier 3 third effect causes Mortal victims to be affected by the Beaten Down Tilt instead. If a mortal\u2019s resistance roll is a dramatic failure then that mortal also gains the Broken Condition. Tier 3 costs 1 additional <i>Pillar (Sheut</i>,<i> Ab, </i>or<i> Ren)</i>.</li> <li><b>Obedient Clay:</b> Tier 3 costs the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Palace Knows Its Pharaoh: </b>Tier 3 costs an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Power of Re:</b> Tier 3 costs 1 additional <i>Pillar (Ab </i>or<i> Sheut)</i>.</li> <li><b>Redacting the Word: </b>Tier 3 costs 1 additional <i>Pillar (Sheut</i>,<i> Ka, </i>or<i> Ren)</i>.</li> <li><b>Rebuke the Vizier:</b> Tier 3 costs an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Revelations of Smoke and Flame:</b> Tier 3 costs the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Rite of the Scarab Minion:</b> Tier 3 costs 1 additional <i>Pillar (Sehut</i>,<i> Ren </i>or<i> Ka)</i>.</li> <li><b>Secrets Stripped from Skies:</b> Tier 3 costs the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Seeds of Life:</b> Tier 3 cost is 1 additional <i>Pillar (Ka</i>,<i> Ren, </i>or<i> Ab)</i>.</li> <li><b>Torn Veil of Fogetting: </b>Tier 3 costs an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Water of Life and Death:</b> Tier 3 cost is the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Word of Amanuensis:</b> Tier 3 costs an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Words of Dead Fury:</b> Tier 3 costs the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> <li><b>Words of Dead Glory:</b> Tier 3 costs an additional 1 <i>Willpower</i>.</li> <li><b>Words of Dead Hunger:</b> Tier 3 cost is 1 additional <i>Pillar</i> <i>(Ren</i>,<i> Ba, </i>or<i> Sheut)</i>.</li> <li><b>Wrathful Desert Power:</b> Tier 3 costs the additional sacrifice of 1 <i>Sekhem</i>.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 01-12-2014, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T12:35:08-08:00","id":47007,"title":"","content":"I'm curious. Are these all GMC update changes, or are your own miscellaneous houserules mixed in? I'm thinking specifically about the changes to third tier utterances and how willpower is spent on affinities. I can't immediately see how those are necessitated by the GMC rules, but it's entirely possible I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're going to require pillars to be spent on affinities, you should probably change the rule that causes a mummy's corpse-form to show any time she spends pillars on anything other than simulating life. Affinities are (mostly) meant to be inconspicuous uses of power, and causing a mummy to go full sybaris-inducing corpse-form every time she uses one is counterintuitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T13:22:15-08:00","id":47029,"title":"","content":"Jacob started his post with saying that they are his GMC update houserules, and there is a healthy amount of houserules in there.<br /> <br /> As far as I could see the GMC conversion on the old forum was more objective (as in only converting the rules).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T09:55:04-08:00","id":47441,"title":"","content":"As Penta notes these are houserules. I'm hoping that an official update will resemble them. One thing I wanted to do was reduce the amount of Willpower spent and increase the amount of Vitae-like energy spent to better align the system with those in Blood &amp; Smoke. Also some of the real god-mode powers like causing an earthquake should cost more energy to invoke presenting players with more dilemmas and giving them a sharper &quot;burning the candle from both ends&quot; gameplay.<br /> <br /> @Gabby, I missed that...as a rule of thumb let's just move the goal line for causing the corpse-form to show through and say it is caused by any expenditure of 2 or more Pillars. That keeps subtle powers subtle and lets earthshaking powers continue to be jarring. On the whole, I'm more concerned with the fitness of the conditions selected for the long-term Sybaris effects. I'm not completely confident that the conditions selected scale well as arranged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:08:10-08:00","id":47446,"title":"","content":"The reason blood and smoke tries to focus on vitae expenditure is because vampires are predators, and they wanted to put them in the position of being corrupted by their powers: the more you use your superspeed, the more you have to feed, the more you have to feed the more you hurt people, the less human you become. <br /> <br /> That is...not really an issue for mummies because that's not how they get their energy. All that ramping up pillar expenditures accomplishes is forcing them to meditate more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T13:50:40-08:00","id":47589,"title":"","content":"Is that a bad thing? <br /> <br /> It takes more than meditation to recover Willpower...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T15:04:02-08:00","id":47631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/28052-mummy-xp-system-and-consistency-with-the-gmc-update?p=47589#post47589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a bad thing?<br /> <br /> It takes more than meditation to recover Willpower...</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing the amount of time players have to have their characters sit in a box and twiddle their thumbs instead of doing interesting things is about as close to an objectively bad decision as can be made, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:03:10-08:00","id":47666,"title":"","content":"Lulz. Depends on what one defines a box as. We can quibble over mechanics forever; ditto for how one judges good vs. bad. I posted my house rules so others could use them as inspirations for their own house rules.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the overall quality of the game experience relies on the the storyteller and players. Mechanics are merely means to an end. Recovering Pillars, like getting more Vitae can be the simple matter of a dice roll and not something that serves as a barrier to doing interesting things. Abstractions like dice rolls are meant to save time, not consume it. <br /> <br /> Doing interesting things is entirely dependent on the troupe as a whole not on some bit of text in a book or online. YMMV.<br /> <br /> From my PoV Mummy is a game of reflection and a number of its systems hang on Meditation, the average character should expect to meditate a bit each day. A clever storyteller can work a good amount of story into meditation itself. Memory, IRL, is a very reflective process, this can be good, you can use meditation time as exposition time and plant all kinds of story seeds. Remember Mummies have really disjointed memories that frequently lack context. This can be a big part of this game. Again YMMV.<br /> <br /> Note I'm not sure what the real quibble is here. Willpower is much harder to get back in this game. In my own games I prefer that players only have to spend it to do non-trivial things (and all Affinities are rather trivial effects). So...YMMV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:39:48-08:00","id":47690,"title":"","content":"Your houserules are your houserules, I'm just expressing my criticisms of their basis. I don't especially like making affinities reliant on pillar expenditure because it requires you to write exceptions into the &quot;When do I go all corpse-y?&quot; rules, which I feel was exactly why they ran off willpower in the first place. Fixing it to any expenditure of 2 pillars in a turn doesn't really help, since there are levels of sekhem where you literally can't spend two pillars in a turn, and also at high sekhem you can get a lot of supernatural mileage out of a single pillar (extremely significant attribute increases, 5 turns of unnatural healing). <br /> <br /> You could change the exception to &quot;any time you spend pillars on anything other than affinities and simulating life&quot; but that then loses a lot of the metaphysical justification for why pillar use reveals you in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:35:47-08:00","id":47783,"title":"","content":"I get that complaint. IMO, it is even better to just contain the corpse-likeness to when Utterances are used and when your Sekhem is high (IIRC you look like a corpse at 8 Sekhem and above anyway), boiling it down to 2 triggers for Terror Sybaris. This aligns better with the apparent intensions of Affinities and Utterances.<br /> <br /> The main problem with Sybaris on the whole is that it is trying to channel both Lunacy and Disquiet. Unease Sybaris/Disquiet is a very kludgey mechanic due to the social nature of WW games. Irrational NPC behavior makes the game more difficult to storytell. Rolling penalties into the Integrity and Humanity mechanics as GMC and B&amp;S have done is a much better way to go. Eliminating dice pool penalties becomes enough incentive for increasing one's Memory (or Humanity in the case of a game like Promethean). The Breaking Point system makes increasing Memory (or sometimes just keeping what you have) enough of a challenge, making extra mechanics like Unease Sybaris or Disquiet seems potentially excessive. One thing I hope the developer re-examines the Unease Sybaris system; it might not be necessary, I'm not certain that it fulfills a necessary role in the game that can't be more easily accomplished through ordinary storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}